From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 05:14:47 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] pinctrl: apple: Let GPIO interrupts be wakeup sources
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Apple GPIO irqchip has no irq_set_wake(), so enable_irq_wake() on
one of its interrupts fails. gpio-keys with wakeup-source calls it from
its suspend callback, and the failure aborts system suspend.

There is nothing to arm: the GPIO bank interrupts are chained to the
AIC, which stays up in suspend-to-idle, and any of them wakes the CPU.
Mark the chip IRQCHIP_SKIP_SET_WAKE.

Signed-off-by: Berkay Kösebay <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
[Orchard: from brkosebay/linux e846959b (J71t ledger 9.4 context); the
 flag was never in Hoolock or Paul Praschl's tree, Berkay added it with
 the Smart Cover buttons. Taken unchanged; it applies to every Apple
 pinctrl SoC.]
Co-developed-by: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Signed-off-by: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/pinctrl/pinctrl-apple-gpio.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pinctrl/pinctrl-apple-gpio.c b/drivers/pinctrl/pinctrl-apple-gpio.c
index f9d444a95..b97023c97 100644
--- a/drivers/pinctrl/pinctrl-apple-gpio.c
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/pinctrl-apple-gpio.c
@@ -392,7 +392,12 @@ static const struct irq_chip apple_gpio_irqchip = {
 	.irq_mask		= apple_gpio_irq_mask,
 	.irq_unmask		= apple_gpio_irq_unmask,
 	.irq_set_type		= apple_gpio_irq_set_type,
-	.flags			= IRQCHIP_IMMUTABLE,
+	/*
+	 * Nothing to arm: the bank interrupts are chained to the AIC, which
+	 * stays up in suspend-to-idle, and any of them wakes the CPU. Without
+	 * this, enable_irq_wake() fails and so does gpio-keys' suspend.
+	 */
+	.flags			= IRQCHIP_IMMUTABLE | IRQCHIP_SKIP_SET_WAKE,
 	GPIOCHIP_IRQ_RESOURCE_HELPERS,
 };
 
